Subject: RFQ — spare parts for gas engine {ENGINE MODEL}, ESN {ESN}

Dear Sir/Madam,

We are sourcing spare parts for a stationary gas engine:
- Engine: {MAKE MODEL, e.g. Cummins QSV91G / Caterpillar G3516C / INNIO Jenbacher J420}
- Engine serial number (ESN): {ESN}
- Genset/module serial number: {MODULE S/N}
- Fuel gas: {natural gas / associated gas / biogas / landfill gas / coal mine methane}
- Operating hours: {HOURS}

Please quote the following positions:
{No. | Part number(s) incl. superseded numbers | Description (EN) | Qty | Unit}

For each position please confirm:
1. Whether you offer GENUINE OEM, OEM-supplier branded, or ALTERNATIVE part — state clearly which.
2. Manufacturer and brand of the offered part.
3. Photo of the part marking (not the box).
4. Country of origin and production date.
5. For spark plugs: electrode type (J-gap / 4-ground / prechamber), electrode material, and expected service life in operating hours.
6. For gaskets and seals: material (NBR / FKM-Viton / MLS) and temperature range.
7. For ignition coils: primary resistance, energy, and compatible ignition controller.
8. Unit price, price for the full quantity, currency and Incoterms.
9. Stock availability and lead time.
10. Return conditions if the part does not fit.

We order in volume and are ready to discuss a volume discount. Please indicate your best price for the full quantity.

Best regards,
{NAME}, {COMPANY}
